#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0070 expect=noViolation domain=LB
#note "NORMALISATION DISCRIMINATOR. Row 1's raw halves are 22 and 16 characters, which a naive length comparison would call different tiers; intervalHalfPrecision strips the UTC offset first, exactly as CalendarDates.isValidDate does, so both measure minute precision and the operator returns false. Row 2 does the same for equal fractional-seconds tails. ESCALATE -- do not re-aim: a violation here would mean the halves are compared before normalisation, contradicting the operator's documented intent that SEND70 asks about the REPRESENTATION of the two halves and not the instant they denote."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset LB class=FINDINGS label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Test Short Name"
col LBDTC    type=Char label="Date/Time of Specimen Collection"
col LBSTDTC  type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Specimen Collection"
col LBENDTC  type=Char label="End Date/Time of Specimen Collection"
---
S1 | LB | 001 | 1 | ALB | 2023-01-15T10:00+02:00/2023-01-15T14:30       |  |
S1 | LB | 001 | 2 | ALB | 2023-01-15T10:00:00.500/2023-01-15T14:30:00.250 |  |
---
